   <front>
     <title>Announcement of a Mail Facility at UCSB</title>
     <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="574" stream="IETF"/>
+    <author fullname="M. Krilanovich" initials="M." surname="Krilanovich">
+      <organization showOnFrontPage="true">UCSB</organization>
+      <address/>
+    </author>
     <date year="1973" month="September"/>
     <abstract pn="section-abstract">
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">There now exists a server program at UCSB, resident under socket 3,
+which supports that subset of the File Transfer Protocol necessary
+for mail delivery.  Only the MAIL and BYE commands are implemented at
+this time.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-2">Mail may be sent to an individual at UCSB by specifying his local
+user name in the MAIL command.  The following is a list of those
+individuals currently defined as valid recipients of Network mail,
+each with their respective user name:  Ed Faeh (FAEH), Jim Guyton
+(GUYTON), Mark Krilanovich (KRILANOV), Curtis Mosso (MOSSO), John
+Pickens (PICKENS), and Ron Stoughton (STOUGHTN).  In addition, any
+general comments or complaints about UCSB services may be sent to
+user name GRIPE.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-3">[ This RFC was put into machine readable form for entry ]
+[ into the online RFC archives by Dave Bachmann 1/98 ]</t>
     </abstract>
